Hi Team

I am currently processing UMI-tagged sequencing data and utilizing fgbio (v3.1.1) for consensus calling (specifically via CallDuplexConsensusReads). I would like to understand the specific BAM tags used to store data regarding consensus read support.
Could you please confirm the standard tags used for the following metrics in the output consensus BAM?
a) Total Family Size: Which tag represents the total number of raw reads collapsed into the consensus?
b) Duplex Status: Is there a specific tag that identifies a read as a Duplex Consensus vs. a Single-Strand Consensus?
c) Per-Strand Support: How does fgbio report the breakdown of Top vs. Bottom strand reads?
d) Consensus Quality

For reference, I have included a few representative records from the consensus BAM generated by your tool below.
